19:T53b,## Publish / subscribe

A spreadsheet cell changes, every chart using it must redraw. A user logs in, the header, the cart, and analytics all need to react. That's a **one-to-many** dependency, and you don't want the source hard-wired to each consumer.

## The pattern

The **Subject** keeps a list of **Observers** (typed as an interface) and offers `subscribe` / `unsubscribe`. When its state changes it calls `notify()`, which loops the list and calls `update()` on each:

```
class NewsAgency {
    List<Subscriber> subs;
    void subscribe(Subscriber s){ subs.add(s); }
    void publish(String news){ for (var s : subs) s.update(news); }   // fan-out
}
```

The agency knows only the `Subscriber` **interface**, never the concrete email/SMS/app classes. New subscriber types plug in without touching it (Open/Closed), and they can come and go at runtime.

## Trade-offs

- **Push vs pull**, send the data in `update(news)`, or just signal "something changed" and let observers pull what they need.
- Watch for **notification storms** and **ordering** assumptions (observers shouldn't depend on call order).
- A subscriber that forgets to unsubscribe is a classic **memory leak** (the lapsed-listener problem).

> This is the engine behind UI event listeners, MVC, and reactive streams (RxJS, signals). "Don't call us, we'll call you."c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-behavioral","activeLesson":"observer"}],["$","$L18","observer",{"lesson":{"id":"observer","patternId":"lld-behavioral","title":"Observer","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Define a one-to-many dependency: when one object changes, all its subscribers are notified automatically, without it knowing who they are.","companies":["Amazon","Meta","Google"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"The wiring","code":["interface Subscriber { void update(String news); }","class NewsAgency { List<Subscriber> subs; void publish(String n){...} }","class EmailSub implements Subscriber { ... }   // + SmsSub, AppSub"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"The NewsAgency (Subject) keeps a list of Subscribers and exposes subscribe() + publish(). It holds them as the interface, never concrete types.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"subj","name":"NewsAgency","fields":["- subs: List"],"methods":["+ subscribe(s)","+ publish(news)"],"x":0.2,"y":0.4},{"id":"obs","name":"Subscriber","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ update(news)"],"x":1.8,"y":0.1,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"email","name":"EmailSub","methods":["+ update()"],"x":1,"y":1.6},{"id":"sms","name":"SmsSub","methods":["+ update()"],"x":1.95,"y":1.6},{"id":"app","name":"AppSub","methods":["+ update()"],"x":2.85,"y":1.6}],"relations":[{"id":"agg","from":"subj","to":"obs","kind":"aggregate","label":"observers","toMult":"*"},{"id":"e","from":"email","to":"obs","kind":"implement"},{"id":"s","from":"sms","to":"obs","kind":"implement"},{"id":"a","from":"app","to":"obs","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["subj","obs"],"shownRelIds":["agg"],"activeIds":["subj"]},"vars":[["knows","Subscriber interface only"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":3,"narration":"EmailSub, SmsSub, AppSub each implement 